# config/privacy-maritime.list.example -- operator-designated maritime privacy list (2026-10-23).
# Install as /etc/corporatetraveldc/privacy-maritime.list (root-owned, 0640; the operator
# account must be able to read it for push-time checks). One entry per line; # comments.
# Read by scripts/leak-guard/privacy_lists.py: matched only in maritime context, reported as
# 'maritime-identifier', values never printed. Missing or empty file = "no entries"
# (reported, never a failure). Real entries never go in this tracked example.
#
# mmsi:<9 digits>    an MMSI, matched only next to an mmsi key or in an AIS CSV MMSI column
# imo:<7 digits>     an IMO number, matched after an imo key, as IMO1234567, or in an IMO column
# name:<vessel name> matched only after vessel / vessel_name / VesselName / ship / ship_name,
#                    or in an AIS CSV VesselName / CallSign column
# Synthetic examples (never real vessels), left commented:
# mmsi:000000000
# imo:0000000
# name:SYNTHETIC VESSEL QQ
